        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "page-template"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Page Template\n\nA page is a graph of pieces. Each piece is a node of a role class (masthead, route, section, settings) and the page is **the pieces in graph order**.\n\nThe Method *Assemble the page* stacks the pieces into one document and writes it into the Detail, the Summary and the Glyph, and sets the graph's shape (the Detail's regular 3:2) and its window. The graph's change event runs it, so adding, removing, reordering or editing a piece redraws the page with no extra wiring.\n\nThe interior sits on an **environment**: a face of its own, joined to the root by an environment edge. A page you read shows none; the pieces you edit it with sit on it.\n\nStart by editing the example pieces. The page you are building is the Detail view. A graph made from this template imports it once and gets the four classes and the Method."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
