        },
        "title": "Section heading",
        "body": "Write the section here. A section is a heading and a body; the body takes paragraphs, bullet lists, sub-headings, bold, inline code and links.\n\nEverything you see on this page is a separate piece you can change on its own.\n\nUse this template when the content is prose. A page graph is a document: its pieces are hidden when browsing, and a Method assembles them into the page the graph lands on. Text decides its own length, so nothing can be placed on a page; where a page needs a way out, it carries a link in the text. A graph whose content is places and connections needs no template: it is a scene already.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          }
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      }
